# Patch 0001 — A1: a reply into a comment the live sidecar lacks must not erase its changes
# Offered back: yes (track-changents survey item A1, 2026-09-03)
# Files: store-io.mjs, cli/track-reply.mjs, cli/track-edit.mjs
#
# Reason: when a live sidecar existed but lacked the thread a reply named, both CLIs
# revived the thread from the `.superseded` park with reviveThreadFromSuperseded, which
# builds a FRESH store with an empty suggestion list and saves it over the sidecar.
# track-reply then saved that store (every pending change and every other comment gone);
# track-edit --thread did it right after recordAgentEdit had saved the new op, erasing the
# very change it had just recorded. The fix adds reviveThreadInto(vaultRoot, file, threadId,
# store), which appends the parked thread to a store the caller already holds, in place and
# without saving; reviveThreadFromSuperseded is rebuilt on it and keeps its behaviour for the
# no-live-store case (its upstream test still holds). The exported addReply signature is
# unchanged. Tests: tools/vendor-patches.test.mjs (P1 cases).
